      "content": "hey so i've been reading a lot about how sports are changing Lately. it seems like there's a massive push to prioritize gender identity over actual biological sex in competitive athletics. from a purely scientific and fairness standpoint, isn't it just common sense that biological sex should be the deciding factor to keep competition fair?",
